Specification repository (AAP-SPEC.md, AAP-BROKER-PROFILE.md, README, examples, JSON Schemas, Internet-Draft sources). No CLI, package, build, or published runnable artifact. scripts/ holds the repository checks that CI runs: the schema and spec-example validator (validate_examples.py, which also runs the AIM naming check, check_naming.py, the implementation-status wording check, check_status_claims.py, the Markdown HTML tag check, check_raw_html.py, and the unit tests, test_*.py) and the token fixture drift gate (generate_examples.py --check). Run both before pushing. The 8-phase /pre-push-review (new-user walkthrough, adversarial corpus, score sanity, concept-explainer, real-world dev-tree scan) is not applicable. Review of spec text happens via PR review; the broker reference implementation and its conformance test live in opena2a-org/secretless.
